*   Event: Event 5.\\n        *   Turn Budget: Needs to fit within 20. Let's allocate 20 turns to this one decisive scene to keep it impactful and focused on the declaration.\\n\\n    *   Wait, the prompt says \\\"assigned_eventsだけをシーン順に一度ずつ割り当てる\\\" (Assign only the assigned_events once per scene in order).\\n    *   There is only one assigned event: `id: 5`.\\n    *   Total turn budget is 20.\\n\\n    *   *Scene 1:*\\n        *   Synopsis: 葵が悠真の隣に寄り添い、莉緒に対して自分たちが恋人同士であることをはっきりと宣言する。\\n        *   Turn Budget: 20.\\n        *   Time Point: 夕方 (Evening) or 放課後 (After school).\\n        *   Location: 学校の廊下 (School hallway) or 屋上 (Rooftop). Let's go with 学校の廊下 (School hallway).\\n        *   Turns: `[5]`\\n\\n    *   `scenes`:\\n        *   `synopsis`: \\\"想いを通わせた二人が、莉緒に対して自分たちの関係をはっきりと宣言する。\\\" (Using chapter synopsis as base).\\n        *   `turn_budget`: 20.\\n        *   `time_point`: \\\"放課後\\\"\\n        *   `location`: \\\"学校の廊下\\\"\\n        *   `turns`: [5]\\n    *   `scene_events`: [[5]]\\n\\n    *   JSON format? Yes.\\n    *   No code fences? Yes.\\n    *   No explanations? Yes.\\n    *   Only scene structure? Yes.\\n    *   Assigned events used once? Yes.\\n    *   No other chapter events? Yes.\\n    *   Total budget matches? Yes (20).\\n    *   Characters added? No.\\n\\n    *Self-Correction during drafting:* The chapter synopsis says \\\"想いを通わせた二人が...宣言する\\\". The event is the declaration itself.\\n\\n    *Refining Scene 1:*\\n    Synopsis: 悠真と葵が互いの気持ちを確かめ合った後、莉緒に対し自分たちの関係を公言する。\\n    Turn Budget: 20.\\n    Time Point: 放課後.\\n    Location: 学校の廊下.\\n    Turns: [5].\\n\\n    *Scene Events structure:* `[[5]]`.\\n\\n    Wait, the `turns` array in `scenes` should contain the event IDs assigned to that scene.\\n\\n    *Final Check of JSON structure:*\\n    `{\\\"scenes\\\":[{\\\"synopsis\\\":\\\"...\\\",\\\"turn_budget\\\":20,\\\"time_point\\\":\\\"...\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"...\\\",\\\"turns\\\":[5]}],\\\"scene_events\\\":[[5]]}`\\n\\n    *Wait, checking th